  "output": {
    "answer": "I don't average the four. In the deck itself, that's a backup slide only pulled out in Q&A — crops as served, crops scored offline, a six-crop consensus proxy, and live lots pooled all measure top-3 differently and don't agree. So on the main line I pick one bar and say plainly which yardstick it is rather than quoting a blended number. The record shows the live-lot number gets its own callout — 65.2% on lots that never auto-locked, stated as 'about 2 in 3' — rather than folding it into lock rate and precision, which get pushed to backup.",
